<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Nov 13.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Nov 13.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on November 12. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		    P/E	 Close</p>
<p>1  Tourism Asset	  3700.00    2.35</p>
<p>2  Portman Min	     373.02    3.50</p>
<p>3  Niugini Min	     251.80    8.28</p>
<p>4  Mayne Nickless	  182.78    2.43</p>
<p>5  T N T		     174.82    1.65</p>
<p>6  Colonial Coml	   121.31    2.22</p>
<p>7  Adel Bton Cement	119.57    1.08</p>
<p>8  Herald Rsc		 95.58    2.50</p>
